ptionality":["Expansion into new markets; increasing online presence"],"margins & cost dynamics":["Not disclosed"],"capex / expansion":["Not disclosed"],"capital allocation":["Debt financing through bank loan facilities"],"risks & watch-items":["Regulatory changes; market competition"],"management quality / tone":["n/a (non-concall source)"],"non-obvious takeaways":["The company's focus on sustainable fashion could provide a competitive edge in the market."],"challenges → beneficiaries & losers":["| — | — | — | — |"]}},"segments":[],"themes":[{"parent":"Consumer & Retail","title":"Quick-commerce, omnichannel & retail expansion","tag":"Consumption","tier":2,"status":"Sharpest short-term","relevance":"","need":"Quick-commerce and value retail are the structural growth engine, and Q1FY27 rewrote the unit-economics model. ETERNAL raised Blinkit's steady-state margin from a 5-6% range to ~6% and set a first-ever 4% GAAP EBIT margin target (after ESOP and depreciation) while capex per store went from INR 1cr to INR 2.5cr (+150%) with NOV/store/day up only 60% and net working capital improving 18 to 14 days - so margin can now drift DOWN while ROCE improves. Growth also decoupled from spend: Blinkit orders +21% QoQ with MTUs above 30mn achieved on LOWER marketing spend and fewer store adds, and management called Q1 the peak of competitive intensity to date. VMM did INR 3,727cr (+18.7%) on 10% SSSG with gross margin up to 28.7% driven by lower promotional spend rather than price hikes, validated a small-format store at the same revenue/sq ft and 'pretty much the same' ROCE as large format (a ~3,000-store national opportunity), and found 20% of its quick-commerce customers had never shopped a Vishal store. SHOPERSTOP swung PAT positive (+INR 5cr vs -INR 4cr) and raised FY27 LFL guidance from 5% to ~6%; ARVINDFASN lifted gross margin 90bps to 56.7% on full-price sell-through with direct channels now 62% of sales; MEESHO cut cost per delivered order ~INR 1 QoQ despite the May 